-Goal: explore unusual predictive/inverse signals in **Australian Powerball and Oz Lotto SEPARATELY**. Standard statistical null expectations do not veto unconventional research. Null results are valid. The original catalog has 62 method families; code released previously covered approximately 12 coded families and 40 variants per game. Do not imply all 62 were coded. Method family includes singleton; every variant is a scientific identity. BOTH TOP and WORST seven from the SAME frozen method/readout are necessary; correlations, ensembles and inverse signals may be explored. Never cull methods automatically by poor performance. Powerball current era 7 of 35 plus Powerball 1 of 20; Oz Lotto follows its distinct game profile. Operator-labelled drawn order remains source-labelled. Two games NEVER pooled.
-
-**Absolute method-facing N-1:** for target T the method can access only draws before T. No outcomes at/after T indirectly via whole-file checksum, filesystem metadata, list length, context fields, seeds, cache, feature history, import, model fitting or nondeterministic selection. Reviewer T-05 oracle must perturb T and later (including equal-length suffixes) and prove every method-visible field/content/view digest is unchanged; audit-only master provenance can vary and is NEVER given to methods. No result-website fetch by ChatGPT or Claude: only the owner's reviewed Lotterywest-GOV updater acquires official draws. PROD uses its reviewed launcher; QA/DEV only checked copies according to their own settings. No unapproved raw outcome exposure, science execution or data-master mutation.
